# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vlax-variant-type-returns-a-symbol — vlax-variant-type answers ARRAY / REAL / ... instead of the integer VARIANT type code
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-vlax-variant-type-returns-a-symbol
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

Found while implementing IntersectWith (cador-intersectwith-missing):

: (vl-load-com)
: (vlax-variant-type (vlax-3d-point 1 2 3))   ; clautolisp => ARRAY

The specification (=** Function Entry: VLAX-VARIANT-TYPE=, Return Values)
says "Integer type code": 0 vlax-vbEmpty, 1 vlax-vbNull, 2 vlax-vbInteger,
3 vlax-vbLong, 4 vlax-vbSingle, 5 vlax-vbDouble, 8 vlax-vbString,
9 vlax-vbObject, 11 vlax-vbBoolean, and 8192 + n for a safearray of type n
(so 8197 for an array of doubles, the result of every point property and of
IntersectWith).

* Cause

=builtin-vlax-variant-type= (=clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp=)
interns the variant's internal type KEYWORD (=:array=, =:real=, ...) as an
AutoLISP symbol instead of mapping it to the VARIANT type code. For an array
variant the element type lives in the inner safearray's type tag, which it
does not consult. Code that tests =(= (vlax-variant-type v) 8197)= or
=(>= (vlax-variant-type v) 8192)= -- the classic idiom -- is always false.

* Proposal

Map the internal tag to the code (and for =:array= add 8192 to the code of
the safearray's element type); check =vlax-variant-change-type= and
=vlax-make-variant='s type argument for the same confusion. The probe
=intersectwith-probe.lsp= writes the vendor's value for an IntersectWith
result (field VARIANT-TYPE).

* Acceptance criteria

- =(vlax-variant-type (vlax-3d-point 1 2 3))= = 8197;
  =(vlax-variant-type (vlax-make-variant 1.0))= = 5; strings 8; integers per
  the vendor default (to confirm).
- Builtins tests for each type.
